       loading/empty/error/content + connection + range recompute), MediaPlayerSource seam,
       InMemoryMediaPlayerSource, MediaPlayerUpdate, MediaPlayerRangePreset (web PRESET_IDS),
       MediaPlayerStrings (P1/S10 facade), MediaPlayerAccessibility, OSLog telemetry seam.
  • MediaPlayerPage.Views.swift    — MediaNowPlayingCard (GlassPanel1), MediaVolumeGaugePanel
       (GlassPanel2 + RadialGauge), MediaPlayerStatCards (4 MetricCards), source/status style.
  • MediaPlayerPage.Sections.swift — MediaVolumeChartPanel (GlassPanel7 + AreaChart),
       MediaSourceChartPanel (GlassPanel8 + PieChart), MediaPlaybackHistorySection (GlassPanel9
       + TSDataTable, 6 cols), MediaHistoryColumns, MediaPlayerLoadingView/EmptyView/ErrorView.
  • MediaPlayerPage.swift          — MediaPlayerPage View (adaptive ScrollView + LazyVGrid; macOS
       regular + iOS compact/regular), MediaPlayerRouteRegistration (hosts the page at the
       .vehicleSystems route in the shell RouteHostRegistry).
  • MediaPlayerPage.Previews.swift — content/empty/loading/error previews (DEBUG only).
  • MediaPlayerPage.Tests.swift    — 22 XCTest cases (formatters, classifiers, projection, model
       phase matrix + wiring, range presets, accessibility).
  • MediaPlayerPage.strings        — the surface i18n table (26 parity + chrome + a11y keys).
Navigation registration + infra:
  • Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift     — owns the page model; chains MediaPlayerRouteRegistration onto
       the route-host registry so the page renders in the shell (sidebar/tabs).
  • Sources/App/AppRouteParser.swift — adds the "/media-player": .vehicleSystems deep-link alias.
  • project.yml + .swiftlint.yml   — add TeslaSync/Features as a source/lint path.
  • Localization/Localizable.xcstrings — folds in the 41 surface keys (validated JSON, 8162 total).
SI / units: the surface formats only at the display boundary (Foundation NumberFormatter/
DateFormatter in MediaPlayerFormat). Volume is a unitless Tesla scale (0…max, default 11) — no
SI conversion applies; durations are ms clocks (web fmtPlayTime). No non-SI value is stored.

